class MlModel(WithMlProject, SeedData):
    """
    A persisted Machine Learning model that can be used to generate ML predictions.
    
    A `MlModel` associates a pipeline with the {@link Feature.Set feature sets} required to generate the input data for
    the pipeline.
    To ensure traceability, models are _immutable_: it is not possible to change the underlying pipeline or the
    feature sets once the model is persisted in the database.
    
    Models can be {@link train trained} and {@link process processed} to generate predictions.
    They can also be {@link deploy deployed} on a population of {@link MlSubject subjects}.
    Once a model is deployed, it is possible to use it to generate predictions for those subjects by invoking
    {@link MlSubject#process} or starting a {@link MlSubject#processBatch prediction job}.
    A model operates at a higher level of abstraction than a {@link MlPipeline}: it does not directly accept
    {@link Data} as an input, but it generates the necessary data based on the {@link MlSubject subjects} and the
    time range on which the predictions are made.
    
    The status of a deployed model is held by a {@link MlModel.Route}; that status can be updated (for example to
    promote a model to "CHAMPION" or on the contrary to "retire" the model and stop using it).
    
